There is one viable Track B formulation after all: hand the solver the paper’s native integer set \(U\) explicitly (after an affine change and input shuffling) and ask for the exact pair \((|U+U|,|U-U|)\). The standard exact method enumerates all pairs—quadratic work—whereas recognizing the bounded-base encoding reduces the count to the paper’s inclusion–exclusion identities. I’m sweeping parameters now to keep the statement readable and the post-insight route below 300 exact operations.
