137276:{"schema_version": 2, "model": "anthropic/claude-sonnet-5", "effort": "medium", "params": {"n": 80, "min_route_operations": 80}, "seed": 5529141, "solved": "solved", "parsed": true, "verify_ok": true, "verify_reason": "ok", "reply": "Looking at this problem, I need to work with the structure A = 29\u00b7v - 89504 where v = x\u2080+x\u2081r+x\u2082r\u00b2+x\u2083r\u00b3, with x_i \u2208 {0,1,2,3}, sum \u2264 5, r=638.\n\n**Key insight:** Since r=638 > 2\u00b73\u00b73=6 (max possible digit sum after addition/subtraction), there's no carrying between digit positions. So:\n- A+A corresponds bijectively to sumset of digit-vectors x+x' (component-wise, no carry)\n- A-A corresponds bijectively to difference-vectors x-x' (component-wise)\n\n**Computing S = |A+A|:**\n\nFor sum-vector s (components s_i \u2208 0..6), with L_i=max(0,s_i-3), U_i=min(3,s_i), feasibility of s = x+x' (with x,x' satisfying digit constraints) reduces to: SL=\u03a3L_i \u2264 5 and T=\u03a3s_i \u2264 10.\n\nSplitting by number k of \"high\" components (s_i\u22654):\n- k=0: all s_i\u22080..3, need T\u226410: count = 256-5 = 251\n- k=1: one high component (excess e=1,2,3), need sum_low\u22647-e: totals give 4\u00d7(54+44+32)=4\u00d7130=520\n- k=2: two high components (e1,e2), need SE\u22644 and sum_low\u22644-SE: 6\u00d7(6+6+3)=6\u00d715=90\n- k=3,4: infeasible (minimum excess exceeds bounds)\n\n**S = 251+520+90 = 861**\n\n**Computing D = |A-A|:**\n\nFor difference-vector d, with P=sum of positive components, N=sum of |negative components|, feasibility reduces elegantly to: P\u22645 **and** N\u22645.\n\nUsing generating function g(z,w)=1+(z+z\u00b2+z\u00b3)+(w+w\u00b2+w\u00b3) per component, expand g^4 via multinomial over (i,j,l) with i+j+l=4, needing cumulative sums F_j(5) = coefficient sum of z^p (p\u22645) in (z+z\u00b2+z\u00b3)^j:\n\nF\u2080=1, F\u2081=3, F\u2082=8, F\u2083=10, F\u2084=5\n\nSumming multinomial coefficient \u00d7 F_j(5)\u00d7F_l(5) over all (j,l) with j+l\u22644:\n\n(0,0):1, (0,1):12, (0,2):48, (0,3):40, (0,4):5,\n(1,0):12, (1,1):108, (1,2):288, (1,3):120,\n(2,0):48, (2,1):288, (2,2):384,\n(3,0):40, (3,1):120,\n(4,0):5\n\n**D = sum = 1519**\n\nVerification: D is odd \u2713 (as required since 0 \u2208 A-A and set is symmetric).\n\n<answer>[861,1519]</answer>", "error": null, "elapsed_sec": 140.98, "http_status": 200, "finish_reason": "stop", "preset": "easy", "escalation_round": 0}
137277:{"schema_version": 2, "model": "x-ai/grok-4.6", "effort": "medium", "params": {"n": 300, "min_route_operations": 130}, "seed": 830218439, "solved": "solved", "parsed": true, "verify_ok": true, "verify_reason": "ok", "reply": "The set \\(A\\) is an affine image of the set \\(X\\) of 6-tuples with entries in \\(\\{0,1,2,3\\}\\) whose coordinates sum to at most 5. Consequently \\(|A+A|=|X+X|\\) and \\(|A-A|=|X-X|\\).\n\nBecause the radix satisfies \\(r\\ge 7\\), every integer in \\(X+X\\) (respectively \\(X-X\\)) has a unique base-\\(r\\) representation with digits in \\(\\{0,\\dots,6\\}\\) (respectively \\(\\{-3,\\dots,3\\}\\)). Thus it is enough to count the admissible digit vectors.\n\nA vector \\(y\\in\\{0,\\dots,6\\}^6\\) lies in \\(X+X\\) if and only if its coordinate sum is at most 10. The number of non-negative integer 6-tuples with sum at most 10 is \\(\\binom{16}{6}=8008\\). Subtracting the 504 tuples in which at least one coordinate is at least 7 yields\n\\[\n|X+X|=7504.\n\\]\n\nA vector \\(z\\in\\{-3,\\dots,3\\}^6\\) lies in \\(X-X\\) if and only if the sum of its positive parts is at most 5 and the sum of its negative parts is at most 5. Grouping according to the number \\(k\\) of strictly positive coordinates and the number \\(n\\) of strictly negative coordinates, and writing \\(W(d)\\) for the number of \\(d\\)-tuples with entries in \\(\\{1,2,3\\}\\) that sum to at most 5, produces the explicit values\n\\[\nW(0)=1,\\quad W(1)=3,\\quad W(2)=8,\\quad W(3)=10,\\quad W(4)=5,\\quad W(5)=1.\n\\]\nSumming the corresponding multinomial coefficients times \\(W(k)W(n)\\) over the admissible range \\(k+n\\le 6\\) yields\n\\[\n|X-X|=27085.\n\\]\n\nThus \\(S=7504\\) and \\(D=27085\\).\n\n<answer>[7504, 27085]</answer>", "error": null, "elapsed_sec": 368.77, "http_status": 200, "finish_reason": "stop", "preset": "medium", "escalation_round": 1}
137278:{"schema_version": 2, "model": "anthropic/claude-sonnet-5", "effort": "medium", "params": {"n": 300, "min_route_operations": 130}, "seed": 264882238, "solved": "solved", "parsed": true, "verify_ok": true, "verify_reason": "ok", "reply": "Looking at this problem, I need to work with the structural representation of A.\n\n## Setting Up the Reduction\n\nSince A = 76\u00b7V + 35459 where V = {x\u2080+x\u2081r+...+x\u2084r\u2074 : x\u1d62\u2208[0,3], \u03a3x\u1d62\u22646}, and r=680 \u2265 2B+1=7, the base-r representation is carry-free, so:\n- |A+A| = |V+V|  \n- |A-A| = |V-V|\n\nThis reduces to counting achievable digit-vectors under sum/difference with digit ranges [0,3] and total-sum \u22646 constraint.\n\n## Computing S = |V+V|\n\nFor sum-vector s (components 0..6, T=\u03a3s\u1d62), with L=\u03a3max(0,s\u1d62-3), H=\u03a3min(3,s\u1d62), using L+H=T, feasibility requires: **T\u226412 and L\u2264\u230aT/2\u230b**.\n\nUsing generating function f(x,y)=\u03a3x^s y^{lo(s)} = Q + R where Q=1+x+x\u00b2+x\u00b3, R=x\u2074y+x\u2075y\u00b2+x\u2076y\u00b3, and expanding P\u2075 = \u03a3 C(5,k) Q^{5-k} R^k:\n\nComputing contributions for k=0,1,2,3 (k\u22654 excluded since T\u226412 forces 4k\u226412):\n\n- k=0: \u03a3_{m=0}^{12} a\u2085,\u2098 = 1024\u221221 = **1003**\n- k=1: 5\u00d7(221+190+150) = 5\u00d7561 = **2805**\n- k=2: 10\u00d7(32+40+30+8+1) = 10\u00d7111 = **1110**\n- k=3: 10\u00d71\u00d71 = **10**\n\n**S = 1003+2805+1110+10 = 4928**\n\n## Computing D = |V-V|\n\nSetting e\u1d62=d\u1d62+3 (\u22080..6), with E=\u03a3e\u1d62, L=\u03a3lo(e\u1d62), same lo/hi functions apply. Feasibility requires: **L\u22646, L\u2264E-9, L\u2264\u230aE/2\u230b** (reduces to L\u2264min(6,E-9)).\n\nUsing same expansion, now condition becomes m\u22659-3k (independent of j) plus j\u22646-k restriction:\n\n- k=0: C(5,0)\u00d71\u00d7357 = **357**\n- k=1: C(5,1)\u00d73\u00d7150 = 5\u00d7450 = **2250**\n- k=2: C(5,2)\u00d79\u00d754 = 10\u00d7486 = **4860**\n- k=3: C(5,3)\u00d717\u00d716 = 10\u00d7272 = **2720**\n- k=4: C(5,4)\u00d715\u00d74 = 5\u00d760 = **300**\n- k=5: C(5,5)\u00d76\u00d71 = **6**\n\n**D = 357+2250+4860+2720+300+6 = 10493**\n\nVerification: D=10493 is odd, as required.\n\n<answer>[4928,10493]</answer>", "error": null, "elapsed_sec": 247.92, "http_status": 200, "finish_reason": "stop", "preset": "medium", "escalation_round": 1}
137279:{"schema_version": 2, "model": "google/gemini-3.1-pro-preview", "effort": "medium", "params": {"n": 300, "min_route_operations": 130}, "seed": 540293568, "solved": "solved", "parsed": true, "verify_ok": true, "verify_reason": "ok", "reply": "To find the cardinalities of the sumset $A+A$ and the difference set $A-A$, we can map the elements of $A$ to integer sequences. \n\nThe elements of $A$ are given by $48 \\sum_{i=0}^6 x_i r^i + 73990$. Because the base $r = 1541$ is much larger than the maximum possible sums and differences of the digits, there are no carry-over effects. We can directly analyze the set $S_0$ of the exponent coefficient tuples $(x_0, \\dots, x_6)$. \nFor $x \\in S_0$, each $x_i \\in \\{0, 1, 2, 3\\}$ and $\\sum_{i=0}^6 x_i \\le 4$. \n\n**1. Sumset $|A+A|$:**\nThe sumset $S_0+S_0$ consists of tuples $y = x + x'$ such that $y_i \\le 6$ and $\\sum_{i=0}^6 y_i \\le 8$. \nThere are $\\binom{8+7-1}{7-1} = \\binom{15}{6} = 6435$ weak compositions of at most $8$ into $7$ parts (or equivalently, exact sums into $8$ parts counting a dummy variable). \nThe only constraint violated in this total is $y_i \\le 6$. If some $y_i \\ge 7$, it can be exactly $7$ (which forces the rest of the elements to sum to at most $1$) or $8$ (forcing the rest to be $0$).\n- For a fixed position out of $7$ to be $\\ge 7$:\n  - If it is $7$, the remaining $6$ components sum to $\\le 1$, yielding $\\binom{1+6-1}{6-1} = 7$ ways.\n  - If it is $8$, the remaining $6$ components sum to $0$, yielding $1$ way.\nThus, we subtract $7 \\times (7+1) = 56$ invalid compositions.\n$|A+A| = 6435 - 56 = 6379$.\n\n**2. Difference set $|A-A|$:**\nThe difference set $S_0-S_0$ consists of tuples $z = x - x'$. A tuple $z$ is valid if and only if all $|z_i| \\le 3$, the sum of its positive parts $P \\le 4$, and the sum of its negative parts (in absolute value) $N \\le 4$.\nWe can count these by choosing how many elements $a$ are strictly positive and how many elements $b$ are strictly negative, out of the $7$ positions. Let $F(k)$ be the number of compositions of at most 4 into exactly $k$ parts, where each part is in $\\{1, 2, 3\\}$.\nWe can easily list these:\n- $F(0) = 1$\n- $F(1) = 3$ (parts: 1, 2, 3)\n- $F(2) = 6$ (parts: (1,1), (1,2), (2,1), (1,3), (3,1), (2,2))\n- $F(3) = 4$ (parts: (1,1,1) and three permutations of (1,1,2))\n- $F(4) = 1$ (parts: (1,1,1,1))\n\nSumming over all possible numbers of positive ($a$) and negative ($b$) coordinates:\n$|A-A| = \\sum_{a=0}^4 \\sum_{b=0}^{4} \\frac{7!}{a! b! (7-a-b)!} F(a) F(b)$\n\nComputing the terms in this sum:\n- For $a=0$: sum is $1\\times1 + 7\\times3 + 21\\times6 + 35\\times4 + 35\\times1 = 323$\n- For $a=1$: sum is $21 + 378 + 1890 + 1680 + 315 = 4284$\n- For $a=2$: sum is $126 + 1890 + 7560 + 5040 + 630 = 15246$\n- For $a=3$: sum is $140 + 1680 + 5040 + 2240 + 140 = 9240$\n- For $a=4$: sum is $35 + 315 + 630 + 140 + 0 = 1120$\n\nAdding them all together, we get $|A-A| = 323 + 4284 + 15246 + 9240 + 1120 = 30213$.\n\n<answer>[6379,30213]</answer>", "error": null, "elapsed_sec": 68.95, "http_status": 200, "finish_reason": "stop", "preset": "medium", "escalation_round": 1}
